# Copy to `.env2`. Git-ignored, like every other env file here.
#
# ## What this file is
#
# The directory project and the deploy's secrets — the author's configuration, not
# a user's. A person running Autorag needs none of this; they need `.env`, which is
# their own corpus project.
#
# ## Why DIRECTORY_ and not SUPABASE_
#
# There are two Supabase projects in this repo and `SUPABASE_URL` does not say
# which. Pointed at the wrong one, the demo counter finds no `demo_usage` table and
# the demo pauses with nothing saying which database was wrong — and every check
# would still pass, because it would be consistently wrong.
#
# So: `SUPABASE_*` in `.env` means the corpus project, `DIRECTORY_*` here means the
# directory, and nothing accepts the other spelling as a fallback. The probes fail
# loudly on the wrong name rather than quietly on the wrong database.
#
# These are also exactly the three names Netlify wants, so `pnpm ask:check` fails
# for the same reason a deploy would.

# The directory project's REST URL, e.g. https://<ref>.supabase.co
DIRECTORY_URL=

# `sb_publishable_…`. Committed into src/rag/directory.ts as well, because every
# client has to reach the directory to resolve a session code. `pnpm dir:check`
# fails if the two disagree.
DIRECTORY_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# `sb_secret_…`. Bypasses row-level security and can read every row of `profiles`,
# which is where other people's project credentials live. Never in client code,
# never in src/, never committed. Used by `pnpm dir:check` and by the Netlify
# Function's usage counter.
DIRECTORY_SECRET_KEY=

# The key the demo endpoint spends. Server-side only: the site is a static export,
# so a key in the bundle is readable by anyone who opens devtools. Set a spend
# limit on it — the ten-answer cap is keyed on a hash of the request address and a
# VPN defeats it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify needs these three, under these names, at
# Site configuration → Environment variables:
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   DIRECTORY_URL
#   DIRECTORY_SECRET_KEY
#
# This file is not read by the deploy. Nothing git-ignored is.
